== 4. Trust boundary (D-035) ==

Q1. Can a cell-side builder steer which commit the runner replays a red at? NO.
    Four independent locks, read in the code and exercised:
    a) scripts/run-builder-host.mjs:643 protectedPrefixes = ["studio/",
       "examples/", ".bisellium/", `${studioRelative}/`], enforced per commit at
       :670-671 over `diff-tree -r -m --root --raw -z --no-renames --no-abbrev`,
       and the path must also be in the HOST brief's Files owned. Rowed at
       packages/commands/src/run.test.ts:910-922
       (/unowned\/protected path: studio\/ci\/forged\.log/).
    b) scripts/run-builder-host.mjs:625 `merge-base --is-ancestor baseCommit
       finalCommit`: the export is append-only, so the host's red-log commit
       cannot be dropped, reordered or rewritten by the cell.
    c) The selector is content-addressed to bytes the host recorded, at a
       host-owned path (run-builder-host.mjs:733). Unique or refuse — no
       nearest/newest/best tiebreak (:734-735, rowed b2a/b2b, mutants
       m2a/m2c/m2d killed).
    d) Source-free guard (:737-739): the anchor's SOURCE tree must equal its
       first parent's, so the identifying commit contributes no source; the tree
       replayed is the builder's own earlier committed state (rowed b2c, m2b).

Q2. Can an implementation-present tree pass as a red's pre-change state? NO.
    The existing assertion-level filter refuses a passing replay — rowed b3a
    ("red 1 did not reproduce its assertion failure at <commit>"), mutant m3a
    killed. A different failure is refused by the new title check — rowed b3b,
    m3b killed. A squash that fuses a red log with source is refused by (d).

Q3. Does admitCurrentRunReceipt re-derive the anchor rather than trust the
    receipt? YES, for every entry whose replayedTree differs from sourceTree:
    packages/commands/src/builder-run.ts:331-337 re-runs the same identification
    from the branch (rebasedRedCommit, :269-284) and refuses any other commit.
    Mutant m4a ("gate trusts the named commit") killed by b4. The gate's and the
    runner's exclusion sets are identical ([studioRelative, ".bisellium",
    ...source_excludes]; builder-run.ts:317 vs run-builder-host.mjs:697-701).

    Independent probe (gate-probe.log, a disposable repo outside the tree,
    driving admitCurrentRunReceipt directly):
      P1 honest rebased receipt                         -> admitted
      P2 on-disk red log tampered after the run         -> REFUSED
         "run_receipt red for behaviour 1 is not the rebased pre-change commit of its log"
      P3 on-disk red log deleted                        -> REFUSED (same)
      P4 receipt claiming replayedTree == sourceTree on a non-anchor commit
                                                        -> admitted (today's unchanged tree rule)
      P5 same with replayedTree omitted                 -> admitted (today's unchanged tree rule)
      P6 replayedTree not the commit's recomputed tree  -> REFUSED
         "run_receipt has an unreachable or mismatched red identity"
    Tampering can only make the gate refuse, never admit. P4/P5 are the
    pre-W-134 rule, which the brief's Receipt section preserves verbatim.

