== 6. Findings ==
F1  minor, a class of 2 (new refusal guards with no row and no mutant).
    Searched: every refusal branch introduced by `git diff master...HEAD` in
    scripts/run-builder-host.mjs and packages/commands/src/builder-run.ts,
    cross-referenced against rows b1-b4 and the nine builder mutants. These two
    are the complete set; the remaining uncovered branch is the I/O path
    "the branch's history could not be read" (:730), which has no deterministic
    trigger.
    F1a scripts/run-builder-host.mjs:741
          if (titles.length === 0) throw refuse("its recorded log has no not-ok title to re-attest");
        Mutated away, all four W-134 rows stay green (x1 SURVIVED). Deleting it
        is a real behaviour change: with titles = [], `titles.every(...)` at :805
        is vacuously true, so the rebased path would silently lose the "same
        failure" check that stands in for the destroyed tree equality.
        The builder declared this (deviation 3) and the reasoning holds: the
        brief fixes four numbered behaviours and the runner enforces that count
        (run-builder-host.mjs:708-709, builder-run.ts:171-182), so a fifth red is
        impossible without amending the spec, and an extra assertion added to
        b2/b3 after the reds were recorded would be implementation-first.
        Remedy belongs in a follow-on: amend the brief with the sub-row, record
        its own red. Not a blocker — the guard is present and correct today.
    F1b packages/commands/src/builder-run.ts:310
          (red.replayedTree !== undefined && !/^tree:[0-9a-f]{40}$/.test(red.replayedTree))
        Also survives mutation (x2 SURVIVED), but behaviourally inert: a
        malformed value can never equal a recomputed `tree:<40 hex>`, so :329
        refuses anyway. Informational, no action.

F2  informational. scripts/run-builder-host.mjs:800 — the direct path's refusal
    message gained " at <commit>". No test in this repo pins the old text
    (searched *.ts/*.mjs/*.md). studio/briefs/W-130.md:483 and :654 plan to
    extend the SAME throw with ": <reason>". Flag for W-130's builder so the two
    edits do not collide.

F3  informational. The gate skips re-derivation whenever replayedTree equals or
    omits sourceTree (probe P4/P5). This is the brief's Receipt section word for
    word and the pre-W-134 rule; forging it requires host-side write, outside
    D-035's cell-side threat model. No action.

F4  informational. The blob id is computed from worktree bytes
    (run-builder-host.mjs:720, builder-run.ts:270) while git's committed blob is
    post-filter. GIT_LOCKDOWN (:82-92) pins filter.lfs.* but not core.autocrlf or
    .gitattributes text filters. Any divergence causes a refusal, never an
    admission. No action on Linux.

